  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report 2025's own Segment Reporting note (IFRS 8), 'The Premier Bank PLC.' Total column (Conventional Banking + Islamic banking branches + Off-Shore Banking Unit, i.e. Solo/Bank basis), cross-confirmed against the report's own 'Performance Highlights for Five Years 2021-2025' table (identical Total Assets 423,551.38, Profit after Tax -9,785.41). IMPORTANT - the FY2024 asset-quality shock deepened sharply in FY2025 into a full-blown crisis: NPL ratio rose further to 31.01% (classified loans 103,893.95m, up from 75,527.14m), CRAR collapsed to 5.70% (roughly half the regulatory minimum-plus-buffer requirement), Interest Expense (29,805.39m) now EXCEEDS Interest Income (23,799.62m) producing a NEGATIVE Net Interest Income of -6,005.77m, Total Operating Income collapsed to just 1,238.42m (from 16,077.26m in FY2024, a 92% decline), and the bank posted a Solo net loss of -9,785.41m (EPS -7.93) versus a small profit of +1,454.59m in FY2024. Total assets and deposits both contracted year-on-year (a rare balance-sheet shrinkage in this series) and Loans now exceed Deposits (LDR 101.70%). Equity nearly halved (27,042.86 to 17,146.71) purely from the loss, but remained positive, so ROE/ROA are meaningful (very negative) numbers, not null, per the negative-equity-vs-negative-earnings distinction. Credit rating was downgraded intra-year (Long-term Local AAA to AA; Short-term ST-1 to ST-2). Reserve fund = Equity 17,146.71 minus Paid-up 12,334.31 = 4,812.40, matching the report's own 'Reserve and Surplus' line exactly. roe_pct/roa_pct calculated on a period-end basis (not average) given the sharp intra-year equity decline, consistent with the schema's 'calculated_period_end_not_average' convention.",
